boot: harb init -- machine qemu_cloud (hosted / x86_64 / qemu_pc) -- pid 1
boot: console /dev/ttyS0
boot: mount proc at /proc -- done
boot: mount sysfs at /sys -- done
boot: mount devtmpfs at /dev -- done
boot: mount cgroup2 at /sys/fs/cgroup -- done
boot: mount ext4 at /data -- done
boot: grant network (effectful)
boot: grant filesystem (effectful)
boot: grant process (effectful)
boot: grant threads (compute)
boot: grant clock (sensing)
boot: network loopback -- lo up 127.0.0.1/8
boot: budget -- ringserv 128 MiB and 100% of a core and 64 tasks; the kernel holds the ceiling, not the world
boot: health -- ringserv every 10s; a world that stops refreshing stops the watchdog
boot: floor -- the machine is not a world's to change: none may mount or unmount, set the clock, load a module, rename the host, make or enter a namespace, trace another process, or reboot the box
boot: start ringserv -- pid N -- /harb ready /run/ringserv.ready 127.0.0.1:8210 --every 2 -- /ringserv run /app/app.ring --data /data
RingServ 0.9.0 — serving on http://127.0.0.1:8210/api/v1  (2 workers)
boot: ringserv -- ready (/run/ringserv.ready)
boot: judge -- the boot matches its expectation (/etc/expected, 18 lines)
boot: --halt-on-verdict: every service is ready and the boot is judged; the court ends what a real init never would
boot: init halts the machine -- reboot(RESTART)
reboot: Restarting system
